<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<handout>
  <title>Function Practice! Sections 1.1 and 1.2</title>
  <alert>MTH 124</alert>

  <activity>
   
      <introduction>
        <p>Let <m>M(t)</m> denote an account balance <m>M</m> measured in dollars on day <m>t</m>.  We'll take <m>t=0</m> to be first day the account was opened.</p>
      </introduction>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>What does it mean to say <m>M(0)=1000</m>?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
        <p>
          The account balance when you initially open the account was $1000.
        </p>
      </solution>
      </task>
      
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>What does it mean to say <m>M(365) = 3000</m>?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            On day 366 (one year later) there was $3000 in the account.
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>If on day 2 of opening the account, the account balance was <m>\</m>1012$, how would you write that in function notation?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            Day 2 is <m>t=1</m>, so <m>M(1) = 1012</m>
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>What does the following statement mean: "<m>M(30) - M(0) = 100</m>"?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            Since <m>t=30</m> is day 31, the account balance 
            changed (went up) by $100 in the first 31 days.
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
  </activity>
  <activity>
   
      <introduction>
        <p>There is a specific breed of bacteria whose global population after <m>t</m> months is given by the function <m>p(t) = 4t^5 + 4t^2+4240.</m></p>
      </introduction>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>What is the population of bacteria after <m>t=6</m> months?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            <m>p(6)=35,488</m> bacteria
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>What does it mean to say <m>p(1) = 4248</m>?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            After 1 month the global population of bacteria is 4,248.
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>How would you find what time the global population was <m>5000</m>?  Set up!  No need to solve!</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            You want to solve <m>p(t)=5000</m>, or <m>5000 = 4t^5+4t^2+4240</m>, and solve for 
            <m>t</m>.  I'd suggest graphing it...
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
  </activity>
  <activity>
      <introduction>
        <p>Consider the graph below for a function <m>y=f(x)</m>.</p>
<image width="35%">
                        <shortdescription>
                            A piecewise function f(x).
                        </shortdescription>
                        <prefigure xmlns="https://prefigure.org" label="prefigure-1-2-7">
                            
                            <diagram dimensions="(250,250)" margins="5">
                              <definition> f(x)= 2 </definition>
                              <definition> g(x)=7/3*x-29/3</definition>
                              <definition> h(x) = -(x-8)+9</definition>
                                <coordinates bbox="[-2,-2,13,13]">
                                    <grid-axes spacings="((-2,1,13),(-2,1,13))" hticks="(-2,1,13)" vticks="(-2,1,13)"  
                                    decorations="yes" hlabels="(2,2,12)" vlabels="(2,2,12)"/>
                                    <graph function="f" domain="(0,5)"/>
                                    <point p="(0,f(0))" fill="blue" stroke="blue" />
                                    <graph function="g" domain="(5,8)"/>
                                    <graph function="h" domain="(8,10)"/>
                                    <point p="(10,h(10))" fill="white" stroke="blue" />

                                </coordinates>
                    
                            </diagram>
                        </prefigure>
                    </image>      </introduction>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>What is <m>f(2)</m>?  <m>f(8)</m>?  <m>f(10)</m>?</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            <m>f(2)=2, \ \ f(8)=9, \ \ f(10)</m> does not exist (DNE)
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>Find all values of <m>x</m> such that <m>f(x) = 4</m>.</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            When <m>x\approx 5.9</m>, that is <m>f(5.9)=4</m>
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      <task workspace="0.7in">
        <statement>
          <p>Find all values of <m>x</m> such that <m>f(x) = 2</m>.</p>
        </statement>
        <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            It's the whole first interval: <m>0\le x \le 5</m>, or <m>[0,5]</m>
          </p>
        </solution>
      </task>
      </activity>
      <activity>
      <introduction>
        <p>A book store has an interesting model for the cost of books, depending on how many you buy.  Let <m>C(n)</m> be a function describing the cost (in dollars) of buying <m>n</m> books, given by the table:</p>
        <tabular>
          <row header="yes" bottom="major">
            <cell><m>n</m></cell>
            <cell>1</cell>
            <cell>2</cell>
            <cell>3</cell>
            <cell>4</cell>
            <cell>5</cell>
            <cell>6</cell>
            <cell>7</cell>
          </row>
          <row>
            <cell><m>C(n)</m></cell>
            <cell>10</cell>
            <cell>19</cell>
            <cell>27</cell>
            <cell>36</cell>
            <cell>42</cell>
            <cell>46</cell>
            <cell>50</cell>
          </row>
        </tabular>
      </introduction>
    <task workspace="0.7in">
      <statement>
        <p>What does it mean to say <m>C(4)=36</m>?</p>
      </statement>
      <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            Buying 4 books costs $36.
          </p>
        </solution>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.7in">
      <statement>
        <p>What is the value of <m>n</m> such that <m>C(n) = 19</m>, and what does it mean in context?</p>
      </statement>
      <solution component="show-soln">
          <p>
            If <m>n=2</m>, then <m>C(2)=19</m>, that is for the 
            cost to be $19 you would have bought to books.
          </p>
        </solution>
    </task>
  </activity>

</handout>
